# Design system

This file is the source of truth for each visual decision: colors, type, spacing
and the shared parts of the user interface (UI). Read it before you change a
screen. If the product has no UI, write "No UI." below and keep the file.

## Colors

<!-- One table for each theme. Each color is a token. Do not put a raw color value
in a component.

| Token | Value | Use |
|---|---|---|
| `--background` | | Page background |
| `--foreground` | | Main text |
| `--primary` | | Buttons, active states |
-->

## Type

<!-- The font families (two at most), the sizes and the weights. -->

## Spacing and layout

<!-- The spacing scale, the screen sizes (breakpoints), the grid. -->

## Parts

<!-- The shared UI parts (for example, buttons, cards, forms) and where they are in the code. -->

## Rules

- Each color comes from a token.
- Text meets the WCAG 2.1 AA contrast level (Web Content Accessibility Guidelines).
- Motion shows a change of state. It respects the reduced-motion setting.
